; Specification: RFC 4006
; Vendor-ID: 0
; Bases: RFC6733, RFC4005 ;; corrected: (RFC4006.py#bases-nasreq)
; Link: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4006.txt


; Type: Application Scope ;; inserted: (RFC4006.py#application-id)
; Name: Diameter Credit Control
; Section: 12.1
; Page: 86
; Application-ID: 4
; Applies-To: 3.*


; Type: Message
; Name: Credit-Control-Request, CCR
; Section: 3.1
; Page: 9
<Credit-Control-Request> ::= < Diameter Header: 272, REQ, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        { Destination-Realm }
        { Auth-Application-Id }
        { Service-Context-Id }
        { CC-Request-Type }
        { CC-Request-Number }
        [ Destination-Host ]
        [ User-Name ]
        [ CC-Sub-Session-Id ]
        [ Acct-Multi-Session-Id ]
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
        [ Event-Timestamp ]
      * [ Subscription-Id ]
        [ Service-Identifier ]
        [ Termination-Cause ]
        [ Requested-Service-Unit ]
        [ Requested-Action ]
      * [ Used-Service-Unit ]
        [ Multiple-Services-Indicator ]
      * [ Multiple-Services-Credit-Control ]
      * [ Service-Parameter-Info ]
        [ CC-Correlation-Id ]
        [ User-Equipment-Info ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-auth-application-id-credit-control)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 3.1
; Page: 9
"The Auth-Application-Id MUST be set to the value 4, indicating the Diameter credit-control application."
    range 4


; Type: Message
; Name: Credit-Control-Answer, CCA
; Section: 3.2
; Page: 11
<Credit-Control-Answer> ::= < Diameter Header: 272, PXY >
        < Session-Id >
        { Result-Code }
        { Origin-Host }
        { Origin-Realm }
        { Auth-Application-Id }
        { CC-Request-Type }
        { CC-Request-Number }
        [ User-Name ]
        [ CC-Session-Failover ]
        [ CC-Sub-Session-Id ]
        [ Acct-Multi-Session-Id ]
        [ Origin-State-Id ]
        [ Event-Timestamp ]
        [ Granted-Service-Unit ]
      * [ Multiple-Services-Credit-Control ]
        [ Cost-Information ]
        [ Final-Unit-Indication ]
        [ Check-Balance-Result ]
        [ Credit-Control-Failure-Handling ]
        [ Direct-Debiting-Failure-Handling ]
        [ Validity-Time ]
      * [ Redirect-Host ]
        [ Redirect-Host-Usage ]
        [ Redirect-Max-Cache-Time ]
      * [ Proxy-Info ]
      * [ Route-Record ]
      * [ Failed-AVP ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#cca-rating-failed-failed-avp)
; AVP: Failed-AVP
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 4.1.3
; Page: 15
"A CCA message with this error MUST contain one or more Failed-AVP AVPs containing the missing and/or unsupported AVPs that caused the failure."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_RATING_FAILED


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-session-id-the-sessions)
; AVP: Session-Id
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.1
; Page: 15
"Each credit-control session MUST have a globally unique Session-Id as defined in [DIAMBASE], which MUST NOT be changed during the lifetime of a credit-control session."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-used-service-unit-tariff-change)
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.1.1
; Page: 17
"When the Diameter credit-control client reports the used units and a tariff change has occurred during the reporting period, the Diameter credit-control client MUST separately itemize the units used before and after the tariff change."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-multiple-services-indicator-first-interrogation)
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Indicator
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.1.2
; Page: 17
"The credit-control client MUST indicate support for independent credit-control of multiple services within a (sub-)session by including the Multiple-Services-Indicator AVP in the first interrogation."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#cca-multiple-services-credit-control-granted-units)
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 5.1.2
; Page: 17
"If the client indicated support for independent credit-control of multiple services, a credit-control server that wishes to use the feature MUST return the granted units within the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP associated to the corresponding service-identifier and/or rating-group."
    text-only
"Both granted unit quotas MUST contain the same Service-Identifier and/or Rating-Group."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#g-s-u-pool-reference-unit-types-differ)
; AVP: G-S-U-Pool-Reference
; Within: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Section: 5.1.2
; Page: 17
"Where multiple G-S-U-Pool-Reference AVPs (section 8.30) with the same G-S-U-Pool-Identifier are provided within a Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP (section 8.16) along with the Granted-Service-Unit AVP, then these MUST have different CC-Unit-Type values, and they all draw from the credit pool separately."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-initial-multiple-services-credit-control-requested-units)
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.2
; Page: 21
"Where the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP is used, it MUST contain the Requested-Service-Unit AVP to indicate that the quota for the associated service/rating-group is requested."
    absent-if CC-Request-Type = INITIAL_REQUEST and not Multiple-Services-Credit-Control/Requested-Service-Unit


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-first-update-request-number)
; AVP: CC-Request-Number
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.2.2
; Page: 25
"The CC-Request-Number of the first UPDATE_REQUEST MUST be set to 1 (for how to produce unique value for the CC-Request-Number AVP, see section 8.2)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-update-multiple-services-credit-control-requested-units)
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.3
; Page: 27
"Where the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP is used, it MUST contain the Requested-Service-Unit AVP if a new quota is requested for the associated service/rating-group."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-update-used-service-unit-each-type)
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.3
; Page: 27
"If several unit types were included in the previous answer message, the used service units for each unit type MUST be reported."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-termination-used-service-unit-each-type)
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.4
; Page: 29
"If several unit types were included in the previous answer message, the used service units for each unit type MUST be reported."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#cca-final-units-consumed-validity-time)
; AVP: Validity-Time
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 5.6.2
; Page: 35
"Naturally, the Credit-Control-Answer message does not contain any granted service unit and MUST include the Validity-Time AVP to indicate to the credit-control client how long the subscriber is allowed to use network resources before a new intermediate interrogation is sent to the server."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-price-enquiry-event-request)
; AVP: CC-Request-Type
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.1
; Page: 42
"A Diameter credit-control client requesting the cost information MUST set the CC-Request-Type AVP equal to EVENT_REQUEST, include the Requested-Action AVP set to PRICE_ENQUIRY, and set the requested service event information into the Service-Identifier AVP in the Credit-Control-Request message."
    values 4 if Requested-Action = PRICE_ENQUIRY


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-price-enquiry-service-identifier)
; AVP: Service-Identifier
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.1
; Page: 42
"A Diameter credit-control client requesting the cost information MUST set the CC-Request-Type AVP equal to EVENT_REQUEST, include the Requested-Action AVP set to PRICE_ENQUIRY, and set the requested service event information into the Service-Identifier AVP in the Credit-Control-Request message."
    present-if Requested-Action = PRICE_ENQUIRY


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-check-balance-event-request)
; AVP: CC-Request-Type
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.2
; Page: 42
"A Diameter credit-control client requesting the balance check MUST set the CC-Request-Type AVP equal to EVENT_REQUEST, include a Requested-Action AVP set to CHECK_BALANCE, and include the Subscription-Id AVP in order to identify the end user in the credit-control server."
    values 4 if Requested-Action = CHECK_BALANCE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-check-balance-subscription-id)
; AVP: Subscription-Id
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.2
; Page: 42
"A Diameter credit-control client requesting the balance check MUST set the CC-Request-Type AVP equal to EVENT_REQUEST, include a Requested-Action AVP set to CHECK_BALANCE, and include the Subscription-Id AVP in order to identify the end user in the credit-control server."
    present-if Requested-Action = CHECK_BALANCE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC4006.dadx#ccr-refund-account-event-request)
; AVP: CC-Request-Type
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.4
; Page: 44
"The credit-control client MUST set CC-Request-Type to the value EVENT_REQUEST and the Requested-Action AVP to REFUND_ACCOUNT in the Credit-Control-Request message."
    values 4 if Requested-Action = REFUND_ACCOUNT


; Type: AVP Table
; Section: 8
; Page: 55
; Columns: Name                    Code   Section   Type           Must   May   S.not   M.not   Encrypt
CC-Correlation-Id                  411    8.1       OctetString    -      M,P   -       V       Yes
CC-Input-Octets                    412    8.24      Unsigned64     M      P     -       V       Yes
CC-Money                           413    8.22      Grouped        M      P     -       V       Yes
CC-Output-Octets                   414    8.25      Unsigned64     M      P     -       V       Yes
CC-Request-Number                  415    8.2       Unsigned32     M      P     -       V       Yes
CC-Request-Type                    416    8.3       Enumerated     M      P     -       V       Yes
CC-Service-Specific-Units          417    8.26      Unsigned64     M      P     -       V       Yes
CC-Session-Failover                418    8.4       Enumerated     M      P     -       V       Yes
CC-Sub-Session-Id                  419    8.5       Unsigned64     M      P     -       V       Yes
